    description: "Half of the owner's 2026-09-01 ruling (a) on WI-livar, scoped with INV-tafig.\nThis is INV-tafig's four artifacts. It ships FIRST of the two axes because\nio-boundary is the ENUMERABLE one, so it instantiates the registry / linter /\nproperty-test shape that the module-key axis then reuses in its lighter form.\n\nSCOPE. ADR-0024 steps 1-4, heavyweight (edge_types.py is the model):\n\n 1. ADR. Numbered, using the ADR-0024 structure. AXIOM, taken VERBATIM from\n    ADR-0049 ruling 1 so that ruling stays the value-level ruling and this\n    becomes the axis it lives on: a boundary value names WHAT DATA CROSSES THE\n    PROCESS BOUNDARY AT THIS CALL SITE, IN WHICH DIRECTION -- not what the\n    program is thereby arranged to do later.\n 2. Registry at packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/io_boundary_types.py:\n    AXIS_* constants, an IoBoundarySpec frozen dataclass (name + axis +\n    description), the tuple of specs, and the accessors all_io_boundary_names()\n    / io_boundaries_on_axis(axis) / find_io_boundary(name).\n 3. Drift linter scripts/check-io-boundary-drift, wrapping axis_drift.find_drift\n    with name_filter=\"IO_BOUNDAR\", wired into .githooks/pre-commit. NOTE: the\n    governance-file rule applies to .githooks/** -- do not self-merge that hunk\n    without approval.\n 4. Property test in packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/: registry invariants plus a\n    live-tree drift assertion.\n Then wire \"io-boundary\" into multi_value_field_axis._known_axes().\n\nTHE VALUE SET IS 19, and the split matters for sectioning. CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES\nis the 17 a catalogue YAML may declare; KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES adds external_potential\n(synthesised by _compute_external_potential, declarable by no catalogue) and\ncommand_launch. A section boundary falls naturally there: catalogue-declarable vs\nsynthesised. _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES (external_potential, command_launch,\nnet_listen) cuts ACROSS that split, so it is per-value metadata on the spec, not a\nsection -- resolve this in the ADR rather than discovering it in review.\n\nSIX CONSUMERS BRANCH ON THE VOCABULARY, one more than INV-tafig recorded at filing\ntime: AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES, _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES,\nverify_claims' KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES validation, cli.py's --io-boundary filter, and\nDEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS, which ADR-0049 added AFTER the item was filed. That\nsixth is the drift the item predicts, so it is evidence and belongs in the ADR.\n\nDONE = the six consumers query the registry instead of module-local constants,\nthe linter fails on a hand-rolled set, and the axiom has a home a per-value ruling\ncan be recorded against. Explicitly NOT in scope: moving any row (that is WI-hazop\ncensus + WI-nosah retag, which this deliberately precedes) and IoPrimitive.boundary's\nown axis comment (that needs the linter-scope fix, filed separately)."  # 2579
    fields: {}  # 2579
