  nonce: 34ae  # 34ae
  message: "DONE in PR #690, merged to dev as 258e7e0879 (rebased, so a new SHA). ADR-0050\nlands the four ADR-0024 artifacts: the ADR, the io_boundary_types.py registry,\nscripts/check-io-boundary-drift, and tests/test_io_boundary_types.py (21 tests),\nwith \"io-boundary\" wired into multi_value_field_axis._known_axes().\n\nVERIFIED ON THE MERGED TREE, WITH A LIVE CONTROL IN THE SAME RUN, not from the\nPR run:\n  io-boundary in _known_axes            True, 19 values\n  CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES                17, order preserved from the hand-written tuple\n  KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES                   19\n  OPAQUE / PRODUCER_OPAQUE              ['subprocess'] / ['command_launch']  (disjoint)\n  _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES            command_launch, external_potential, net_listen\n  check-io-boundary-drift, live tree    exit 0\n  CONTROL, planted offender             FIRES -- reports totally_bogus, not fs_read\n13,045 tests pass, 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean.\n\nTHE AXIOM IS ADR-0049 RULING 1 VERBATIM, not a new sentence: a boundary value\nnames WHAT DATA CROSSES THE PROCESS BOUNDARY AT THIS CALL SITE, IN WHICH\nDIRECTION -- not what the program is thereby arranged to do later. Two axioms\nfor one vocabulary would be the same one-fact-two-homes shape this vocabulary\nalready paid for twice.\n\nFOUR SECTIONS. data_crossing (15), opacity (subprocess, command_launch),\ndeferred_crossing (net_listen), speculative (external_potential).\ndeferred_crossing is a SECTION rather than a violation: net_listen is precisely\nwhat the axiom's second clause excludes, and ADR-0049 created it deliberately.\ncatalog_declarable and counts_in_headline stay PER-VALUE because both cut across\nthe partition -- subprocess is opaque AND counted, so an axis query would need\nexactly one special case.\n\nTHE DISCLOSED NEGATIVE, because a clean linter here means less than it looks.\nDeriving io_boundary.py's five constants from the registry removed the last\nstring-literal set the shared AST walker can see, so the BOUNDAR-filtered scan\nnow collects ZERO assignments and exits 0 over an empty collection -- it would\nexit 0 identically if it were broken. Handled two ways rather than hidden:\ntest_the_drift_scanner_actually_fires proves non-vacuity against a synthetic\ntree, and the three DICT consumers the walker structurally cannot see\n(taint.AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, io_boundary.DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS,\nio_boundary._READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY) get explicit registry-membership\nassertions. Widening the walker serves all four axes and is filed as WI-jinuj.\n\nFOUND WHILE DOING IT: ADR-0016's \"controlled vocabulary\" table documents NINE of\nthe nineteen values. The registry's descriptions are sourced from the shipped\ncatalogue rows and consumer code instead. Also filed as an OPEN QUESTION in the\nADR, unanswered and with no row moved: `logging` is the one data_crossing value\nnaming a PURPOSE rather than a medium and it overlaps ipc_send on stdout (go\nfmt.Println and haskell Prelude.putStrLn are logging; stdout.write is ipc_send),\n46 rows across 12 catalogues.\n\nNOT IN THIS PR, and the reason: the .githooks/pre-commit wiring for the new\nlinter is a governance-file edit needing human approval, so the CI-side property\ntest is the live gate today and the pre-commit convenience line is pending.\nIoPrimitive.boundary still carries no axis comment -- that needs WI-mubup, which\nwidens DEFAULT_CORE_FILES to io_boundary.py. INV-tafig therefore stays VIOLATED\nuntil WI-mubup lands; this item closes on its own four artifacts."  # 34ae
